CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ direct-initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ copy-initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ list-initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ deduced type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ same specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ static data member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
These variables are instantiated while function bodies are type-checked,
after the dynamic initialization procedure was built.  Their value, a
constructor call, stayed the initial value, and __CPROVER_initialize
assigned that code to the object (a type-inconsistent assignment that
failed --validate-goto-model).  The variables registered since are now
added to the dynamic initialization.
